evaluation "qccd-noise@3"
title "The Helios nominal noise model"
about "What Goal 3's architectures are judged by: the team's Helios Nominal Noise Model (QCCD simulation specification, 2026-11-05, based on Jaewon's noise model). Every gate, readout and preparation carries the model's Stim probability. A two-ion gate also pays for the heat it meets above the cooled state. An ion's idle window, however long, dephases once. Transport has no qubit error of its own: it costs time, which the idle channels charge, and heat, which the two-ion gate charges."
include "metrics"
clock "helios"

# The knobs.  The official model is scale 1 with heating priced.
param scale = 1                     # every probability is multiplied by this (0: noiseless)
param heating = true                # price the heat a two-ion gate meets

# Section 1.  r = 1 - F_avg, and Stim's p is 3r/2 on one ion, 5r/4 on a pair.
param r_1q = 1.38e-5
# 5.5e-4 less the 1.1e-5 cooling leaves in the idle channel, since pre-gate cooling is counted in
# the idle window (Sec. 3): the model's "2Q cooled, excluding cooling dephasing", p ~ 6.74e-4.
param r_2q = 5.5e-4 - 1.1e-5
# Leakage is folded separately, as 0.75 of the per-ion probability; a pair's is halved first.
param leak_fold = 0.75
param leak_1q = 1.12e-5
param leak_2q = 2.4e-4
param p_reset = 5e-5
param p_readout = 4.3e-4
param p_crosstalk = 7.2e-5

# Section 2.  Mixed dephasing over one idle window.
param t_lin = 183.28657936          # seconds
param t_g = 3.79487660              # seconds
# "Idle leakage uses the transport-layer rate from Jaweon's report folded by a factor of 0.75" (Sec. 10b).
# The model does not print the rate.  The report gives 1.45e-3 per ion at 200 ms before the Stim
# conversion, which is 4.0e-4 per ion per 55 ms layer (4.0e-4 x 200/55, rounded), and folds it by 0.75
# in DEPOLARIZE1, as below (confirmed by the model's author, 2026-11-07).  It is also Helios's rate
# (arXiv:2511.05465 Sec. III B4, the leakage part of its linear memory term), and t_lin is the rest.
param leak_transport_per_s = 4.0e-4 / 55e-3

# Section 4.  The excess above the cooled state, in Stim p.
param slope = 9.5e-4

define idle_s(i, o) = waited(i, o) * 1e-6

channel prepare "The first preparation"
  about "Every ion starts in |0>, prepared as a reset is, with a reset's error."
  source "Helios Nominal Noise Model Sec. 1 (physical prep / reset, 5e-5: R then X_ERROR)"
  after p in preparations:
    X_ERROR(min(1 / 2, scale * p_reset)) on ions(p) counted as reset

channel idle_dephasing "Mixed dephasing over an idle window"
  about "When an operation reaches an ion, the ion has waited since its last one, through transport, cooling and everything done to other ions. The whole window dephases once: the Gaussian term goes as the square of the total time, so taking the window's steps apart would understate it."
  source "Helios Nominal Noise Model Sec. 2 (Z_ERROR: pZ(t) = 0.5 [1 - exp(-t/T_lin - (t/T_g)^2)])"
  before o in qubit_operations, i in ions(o):
    Z_ERROR(min(1 / 2, scale * 0.5 * (1 - exp(0 - idle_s(i, o) / t_lin - pow(idle_s(i, o) / t_g, 2))))) on i

channel idle_leakage "Leakage over an idle window"
  about "The transport-layer leakage rate of the report the model is based on, 4.0e-4 per ion per 55 ms, folded by 0.75 and charged over the same window in proportion to its length."
  source "Helios Nominal Noise Model Sec. 2; the rate from the report it is based on (Sec. 10b): 1.45e-3 per ion at 200 ms, so 4.0e-4 per 55 ms, as in arXiv:2511.05465 Sec. III B4"
  before o in qubit_operations, i in ions(o):
    DEPOLARIZE1(min(3 / 4, scale * leak_fold * leak_transport_per_s * idle_s(i, o))) on i

channel readout_z "A wrong readout"
  about "Symmetric readout: the outcome is wrong with this probability."
  source "Helios Nominal Noise Model Sec. 1 (symmetric readout, 4.3e-4)"
  before m in measurements where basis(m) = "Z":
    X_ERROR(min(1 / 2, scale * p_readout)) on ions(m) counted as measure

channel readout_x "A wrong readout, in the X basis"
  about "The same flip, for the experiment's own readout of an X memory."
  source "Helios Nominal Noise Model Sec. 1 (symmetric readout, 4.3e-4)"
  before m in measurements where basis(m) = "X":
    Z_ERROR(min(1 / 2, scale * p_readout)) on ions(m) counted as measure

channel ms "The two-ion gate"
  about "The cooled gate's error, plus the excess above the cooled state: every quantum of heat the pair has gathered since its last cooling, background and transport alike, the hotter ion's. The excess goes inside the same depolarizing channel."
  source "Helios Nominal Noise Model Sec. 1 (2Q cooled, excluding cooling dephasing) and Sec. 4 (p_2Q = p_baseline + slope * max(n_gate - n_cal, 0))"
  after g in two_qubit_gates:
    DEPOLARIZE2(min(15 / 16, scale * (5 / 4 * r_2q + (if heating then slope * gate_nbar(g) else 0)))) on ions(g)
      counted as ms_base = 5 / 4 * r_2q,
                 ms_heating = if heating then slope * gate_nbar(g) else 0

channel ms_leakage "Leakage from the two-ion gate"
  about "Applied apart from the gate's own depolarizing channel: the pair's leakage, halved, then folded, on each ion."
  source "Helios Nominal Noise Model Sec. 1 (2Q leakage, folded: 9e-5 on each target)"
  after g in two_qubit_gates:
    DEPOLARIZE1(min(3 / 4, scale * leak_fold * leak_2q / 2)) on ions(g)

channel gate_1q "A one-ion pulse"
  about "Every physical pulse. A frame change is virtual here, so it fails no more than it takes time, and an identity is no pulse at all."
  source "Helios Nominal Noise Model Sec. 1 (1Q computational, p = 3r/2 = 2.07e-5)"
  after g in single_qubit_gates where gate(g) != "I" and gate(g) != "VZ":
    DEPOLARIZE1(min(3 / 4, scale * 3 / 2 * r_1q)) on ions(g)

channel gate_1q_leakage "Leakage from a one-ion pulse"
  about "Folded, and applied apart from the pulse's own channel."
  source "Helios Nominal Noise Model Sec. 1 (1Q leakage, folded: 8.4e-6)"
  after g in single_qubit_gates where gate(g) != "I" and gate(g) != "VZ":
    DEPOLARIZE1(min(3 / 4, scale * leak_fold * leak_1q)) on ions(g)

channel residual_drive "Residual drive on inactive zones"
  about "On a machine whose gates share one global drive, a layer of pulses reaches the qubits sitting it out, at a fraction of the strength. The machine's 1q_gate says how much that costs each of them; on any other machine it says 0. A layer that names one ion is the shim charge a reconfiguration opens with, or too small to count."
  source "QCCD Transport Architectures deck, WISE T9 (arXiv:2305.12773 Sec. V B: below 1e-5 at epsilon ~ 0.1, the bound used as the value)"
  after k in steps where kind(k) = "gate" and duration(k) = primitive("1q_gate", "us") and count(j in operated(k)) > 1:
    DEPOLARIZE1(min(3 / 4, scale * primitive("1q_gate", "residual_inactive"))) on {i for i in ions where i not in operated(k)}

channel reset "A wrong reset"
  about "A reset leaves its ion in |1> instead of |0> with this probability."
  source "Helios Nominal Noise Model Sec. 1 (physical prep / reset, 5e-5)"
  after r in resets:
    X_ERROR(min(1 / 2, scale * p_reset)) on ions(r)

channel crosstalk "Measurement crosstalk"
  about "Each measured ion disturbs every other ion on the chip, its spectators. A mid-circuit measurement and its reset share one crosstalk input, so a reset adds none. The model gives 7.2e-5 per spectator and does not say how ions measured in parallel combine. Here that is a simulation assumption: weak, independent scattering, so each measured ion adds the same 7.2e-5, to first order, wherever the spectator sits relative to the measurement light. Reading out in parallel therefore earns no discount."
  source "Helios Nominal Noise Model Sec. 1 (measurement crosstalk and combined MR crosstalk, 7.2e-5 per spectator)"
  after k in steps where kind(k) = "measure":
    DEPOLARIZE1(min(3 / 4, scale * p_crosstalk * count(j in operated(k)))) on {i for i in ions where i not in operated(k)}
